IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra1-three-valued`
IMPORT `wra1-sch2`

-- Tests for wra1-sch2.l4 (Schedule 2). Every expected value is written by hand from the text quoted in the module, beside the
-- assertion. A figure such as 500 is an invented test figure: the Act supplies none of these amounts.

§ `sch 2 -- the host provisions that now include universal credit`

-- Children Act 1989: "of universal credit (except in such circumstances as may be prescribed)": in the prescribed circumstances it is out

#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17(9)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17(9)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17(9)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17A(5)(b)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17A(5)(b)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 17A(5)(b)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 29(3) and (3A)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 29(3) and (3A)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 s 29(3) and (3A)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 Sch 2 para 21(4)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 Sch 2 para 21(4)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` `sch 2 CA1989 Sch 2 para 21(4)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

